              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">6. Summary & Quantitative Trading Takeaways</h2>
        <div class="bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800 rounded-xl p-6 text-slate-300 space-y-3">
          <p class="font-semibold text-white">Production Quant Guidance:</p>
          <p>1. <strong>Ideal for FX and Crypto:</strong> Vanna-Volga is the industry standard because market quotes are provided in Delta space ($25\Delta$ RR and BF).</p>
          <p>2. <strong>Clamp extreme wings:</strong> For extreme tail strikes ($10\Delta$ and below), parabolic expansion can produce unphysical volatilities. Implement a linear extrapolation flat wing beyond the 10-Delta bounds.</p>
          <p>3. <strong>Exotic Barrier Pricing:</strong> When pricing one-touch or knock-out barrier options, adjust the Vanna-Volga correction with survival probability weights to avoid overpricing barrier hedge slippage.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
